+Reject duplicate/concurrent reservation, wrong participant/offer revision, invalid recipient network, unsupported manifest, fingerprint mismatch, live deployment mismatch, missing/stale/cross-role allocation result, wrong key/destination/commitment, stale/wrong-role/wrong-loan/mismatched candidate approval, expired or cancelled draft, and any dependent artifact that does not bind exactly. A hashed-field change creates a new candidate version/hash and invalidates all prior candidate approvals. Duplicate identical approvals and commitment retries return the same durable result; concurrent final approvals commit at most once. Pre-activation amendment creates a later version and fresh dependent artifacts; cancellation is terminal for that reservation. These rules prevent an apparently successful retry from reviving old approval or signing material.
 
